        <!-- 4. Compare table. #compareTable and js/compare.js untouched.
             ITS TIER CLASS IS DEFERRED TO B5, and the reason is the same boundary
             this batch already draws for the two plates and the Our Work mosaic:
             B4 tiers the sections it AUTHORS, B5 tiers the sections that survive
             (Jen §3.2 — her §2.1 table is "the assignment of record" for B5).
             The measurement made the boundary load-bearing rather than tidy.
             Re-tiering a surviving section changes only its class attribute, so
             the diff is a removed/added pair on one <section> whose children all
             match — and neither half can be named: `class="container"` is a
             substring of four sibling sections in the baseline, so any entry for
             it is held in check by its count alone, which is exactly the lazy
             declaration the specificity check exists to reject. Adding the class
             in B5, where the whole page is re-tiered at once, is declarable. -->
        <section class="container">
